Z||000000||LT1 Chop Top||08-20-2001||11:45 PM||||OK,<P>I got the wheel off......NOW my new wheel has several wires to hook up the horn, and post has no wires!  (See pics)  Now what??????<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Wheel1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wheel_2_1.jpg"> <P>Thanks for the help!||||reg||5
Z||000001||84Bill||08-21-2001||08:35 AM||||There is a small plastic insert that goes into one of the small holes in the wheel hub. I may have one at home I can get a picture of later.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-21-2001||01:23 PM||||the center tab/or wire on new button connects to stock wire coming thru hub. You have to ground another wire on button somewhere inside hub. some buttons have a spring clip around the outside that grounds it.<P>the stock wire connects to a small plastic and brass piece that sticks up just to the upper left of the steering shaft inside the hub.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||1
